  "prefLabel": "Plc 313.30 Substantially Similar Requirements for the Profession Regulated by the Installation Standards Board",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 313.30 Substantially Similar Requirements for the Profession Regulated by the Installation Standards Board. For purposes of obtaining a license by endorsement as a manufactured housing installer, as regulated by the installation standards board, the current requirements of the licensing jurisdiction shall be as follows:\n\n(a) Complete a course or training on installation standards for manufactured housing that is approved by the licensing jurisdiction or by the U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development.\n\nSource. #13954, eff 5-3-24 (see Revision Note #1 at part heading for Plc 313)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc300.html"
